"description":"New major release that breaks compatibility with 2.x\r\n\r\n- PHP5.4.19+\r\n- New ORM & behaviors.\r\n- Improved Routing\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":11,"created_at":"2014-08-13T15:06:37Z","updated_at":"2014-08-14T14:13:22Z","closed_at":"2014-08-14T14:13:22Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Just playing a bit with the new ORM (3.0.0 a2) and found this issue:\n\nput a functions in the `TagsTable.php` that is supposed to return all tags that are not linked to products with a certain condition:\n\n```\npublic function getUnlinkedTags($channel_id) {\n    $linked_tag_ids = $this->find();\n    $linked_tag_ids\n        ->select(['id'])\n        ->matching('Products', function($q) use ($channel_id) {\n            return $q->where(['Products.channel_id' => $channel_id]);\n        });\n    $query = $this->find();\n    $query->where(['id NOT IN'=>$linked_tag_ids]);\n\n    $tags = $query->all();\n\n    return $tags;\n}\n```\n\nIf I run this function from a **clean** function in the products-Controller everything is fine. If however I run it from a function that does a little query before\n\n```\n$query = $this->Products->find();\n$query->where(['Products.id'=>$id]);\n$query->contain([\n    'Channels',\n    'Tags'\n]);\n$product = $query->first();\n```\n\nand then run this function it messes up the sql of the inner join (just showing the SubQuery):\n\n```\nSELECT Tags.id AS `Tags__id` \nFROM tags AS Tags \nINNER JOIN products Products ON Products.channel_id = 2 \nINNER JOIN tags_products TagsProducts \nON (Products.id = (TagsProducts.product_id) AND Products.id = (TagsProducts.product_id))\n```\n\nmy fault? So, do I need to reset the query builder?\n","closed_by":{"login":"lorenzo","id":37621,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo","html_url":"https://github.com/lorenzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/4253/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/4253/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}